LLVMSupport: build against the C kit's libc++ (no iostreams, no
random_device) and Picolibc headers

Failure: with the LLVM profile of the C++ runtime (scripts/build-cxx-runtime.sh,
localization, random_device and filesystem off) LLVMSupport does not compile:
`use of undeclared identifier 'tolower'` (APFloat.cpp:3172, CachePruning.cpp:112)
and 'isupper' (RISCVISAInfo.cpp:646,710) which libstdc++ supplies transitively;
ARMBuildAttrs.cpp includes <iomanip>/<sstream> it does not use, and libc++ refuses
iostreams without localization; raw_os_ostream.cpp is a raw_ostream over
std::ostream; raw_socket_stream.cpp includes <sys/socket.h>, which the kit lacks,
yet also holds raw_string_ostream::write_impl, which everything needs;
`Exit code EX_IOERR not available` (ExitCodes.h:30: no <sysexits.h>);
`no type named 'random_device'` (LockFileManager.cpp:306).
Change: include <cctype> where it is used; drop ARMBuildAttrs' two unused
includes; on CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME ABSD leave raw_os_ostream.cpp out (as an
optional source) and build only raw_string_ostream from raw_socket_stream.cpp;
EX_IOERR = 74 under LLVM_ABSD_KIT as for z/OS and Windows; LockFileManager's
backoff jitter seeded from sys::Process::GetRandomNumber() under LLVM_ABSD_KIT.
Behaviour preserved: every other configuration compiles the same code (the
includes are no-ops where they were transitive); raw_os_ostream and
raw_socket_stream are not used by clang or lld (no reference in clang/lib,
clang/tools/driver or lld outside clang Format/Tooling, which clang does not
link); the jitter's randomness source changes, not its distribution.
Upstreamability: the <cctype> and ARMBuildAttrs hunks are plain
include-what-you-use fixes, upstreamable as is; moving raw_string_ostream
out of raw_socket_stream.cpp is an upstream cleanup (upstream later did
so); the rest needs an ABSD target OS in LLVM first.

